# What must not enter the build context.
#
# `node_modules` and `dist` are the load-bearing entries. The Dockerfile installs
# and builds in its own layers, and `COPY . .` runs after both — so a host
# `node_modules` copied in would overwrite the container's install with one
# resolved on a different machine, and a host `dist` would let a stale build
# survive a source change. Neither failure announces itself.

node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
.turbo
**/.turbo
build
.next
**/.next

.git
.github

# Secrets. `.env.example` is committed and carries no values; `.env` does.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Not needed to build or run.
docs
scripts
*.md
!README.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
